# RDX, the same single point with samQEq supplying the charges: ReaxFF's own charge step is disabled
# (checkqeq no) and fix qeq/sam solves with ReaxFF's electronegativities, hardnesses and shielding
# parameters (rdx.param, from make_params.py), the cube-root kernel, the same taper to 10 A and one
# global neutrality constraint. `cutoff on` selects the taper-cutoff operator with no reciprocal part.
# coul/long and pppm/samqeq are present only because the long-range route reads g_ewald from the kspace
# style, and both are switched off (`compute no`); with the fix's own energy excluded, pe and the forces
# are those of ReaxFF alone. Omitting any of the three leaves the charges right and pe and forces wrong.
units           real
atom_style      charge
read_data       data.rdx
pair_style      hybrid/overlay reaxff control.reax_c.rdx checkqeq no coul/long 10.0
pair_coeff      * * reaxff ffield.reax C H O N
pair_coeff      * * coul/long
kspace_style    pppm/samqeq 1.0e-5
kspace_modify   gewald 0.30
neighbor        2.5 bin
neigh_modify    every 10 delay 0 check no
fix             chg all qeq/sam 1 0.0 10.0 1.0e-10 rdx.param
fix_modify      chg cutoff on
fix_modify      chg energy no           # pair reaxff already carries the charge-equilibration energy
pair_modify     pair coul/long compute no
kspace_modify   compute no
compute         reax all pair reaxff
variable        ereax equal c_reax
thermo_style    custom step pe v_ereax
thermo_modify   format float %.10f
run             0
print           "ereax ${ereax}" file energies_rdx_samqeq.txt screen no
write_dump      all custom charges_rdx_samqeq.dump id type q fx fy fz modify sort id format line "%d %d %.15g %.12g %.12g %.12g"
